Please forward to your members if you think they'd be interested.

Just a reminder to register now for Gelato ICE: Itanium(r) Conference & Expo
to be held on October 1-4, 2006 at the Biopolis in Singapore. Early Bird
discount and hotel special rates end September 1. Details are available at
<www.ice.gelato.org>.

Gelato ICE is the world's only conference for Linux(r) on the Intel Itanium
architecture. This event is sponsored by HP, Intel, and the Itanium(r)
Solutions Alliance.

International experts will speak on topics such as: optimization,
scalability, compilers, and grids. New for Gelato ICE Singapore are sessions
targeting multi-core programming and an Itanium(r) Solutions Alliance
software developer track. Keynotes are underway. Steve Geary from HP will
discuss ideas for harnessing the power of the world's largest Linux/Itanium
community. Cameron McNairy from Intel will present an exploration of systems
and software built around Itanium processors.

